# Tests

Primary seam is the external WebSocket protocol against a real temporary PostgreSQL (spec 0001). Test observable behaviour, not private functions.

## Setup

- Require `CALCRON_TEST_DATABASE_URL`; `t.Skip` when unset.
- Boot `server.New` + `httptest.NewServer(s.Handler())`; dial admin, then app.
- Use a unique namespace per test (`time.Now().Format(...)`) so tests don't collide.

## What to assert

- Schedule/workflow/delivery/ack/signal behaviour through protocol replies and received deliveries.
- Idempotency: send the same key twice, assert the original result returns and only one transition exists.
- At-least-once: disconnect before ack, assert the same delivery ID returns on reconnect.
- Correlation isolation: concurrent instances waiting on the same event, different keys.
- Calendars across timezone boundaries, overrides, DST, and each missed-occurrence policy.
- Permission boundaries: admin-only publish, app-scoped authorisation.
- Never log token values in failures.

## Style

- `t.Helper()` in dial/read/write/delivery helpers.
- One runnable check per non-trivial branch, loop, or parser.
- Tests must survive internal refactors — describe behaviour, not implementation. If a test breaks on a refactor, it was testing past the interface.
- Query-plan checks for due-work and pending-delivery before performance work.
